TYPE="glossary"
SCOPE="project-wide"

PURPOSE:
Terminology, file-type conventions, and anti-synonyms for this project.
Loaded every session as Tier 1. Keep entries short and precise.

---

FILE_TYPES:
- .{{AI}}ai  AI-facing: memory, state, decisions, experiments, continuity.
            Written by AI. Read by AI. The human should not need to read these.
- .hey{{HUMAN}}    Human-facing: worksheets, test reports, Q&A input.
            Written by the human. Read by AI every session start.
- .md       Software/repo docs: README, CHANGELOG, roadmaps, human-facing reference.
            Exception: CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md are fixed names required by tooling.

ANTI_SYNONYMS:
- Do not call .{{AI}}ai files "markdown" — they use the AI artifact (#{{AIHEADER}}:1) header format.
- Do not call WORKSHEET.hey{{HUMAN}} a "log" — it is the human's input channel.
- Do not call AI_HANDOFF.{{AI}}ai the "project cartridge" — readme_AI.{{AI}}ai is the cartridge.
- Do not call ai_context/ files "documentation" — they are AI continuity state.

---

KEY_TERMS:
- THREAD        A named unit of ongoing work (THR-NNN). Has status and tier.
- HANDOFF       A session-end summary written for the next AI instance.
- CARTRIDGE     The readme_AI.{{AI}}ai file. Source of truth for active project state.
- TIER 1        Files loaded every session (budget-constrained, always present).
- TIER 2        Files loaded on demand (no size cap; selective loading only).
- STOP-THE-LINE Mandatory execution pause when a material issue is detected.
- HI MODE       High-Integrity operating kernel. Truth > momentum.
- TASK CONTRACT Required pre-work fill-in before any code change.
- ZOOM LEVEL    Strategic | Tactical | Operational — scope of current session.
- SKI LIFT      Cross-project tooling pattern worthy of standardization.

